body: 
[
The t-test was invented to analyse small medical experiments @student1908. R still includes one of the original datasets, #NormalTok("sleep");: the extra hours of sleep that 10 patients gained with each of two sleeping drugs. Because the #emph[same] patients took both drugs, this calls for a #strong[paired] t-test:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("drug1 ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" sleep");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("extra[sleep");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("group ");#SpecialCharTok("==");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("]");],
[#NormalTok("drug2 ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" sleep");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("extra[sleep");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("group ");#SpecialCharTok("==");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok("]");],
[#FunctionTok("t.test");#NormalTok("(drug2, drug1, ");#AttributeTok("paired =");#NormalTok(" ");#ConstantTok("TRUE");#NormalTok(")");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([],
[#NormalTok("    Paired t-test");],
[],
[#NormalTok("data:  drug2 and drug1");],
[#NormalTok("t = 4.0621, df = 9, p-value = 0.002833");],
[#NormalTok("alternative hypothesis: true mean difference is not equal to 0");],
[#NormalTok("95 percent confidence interval:");],
[#NormalTok(" 0.7001142 2.4598858");],
[#NormalTok("sample estimates:");],
[#NormalTok("mean difference ");],
[#NormalTok("           1.58 ");],));
]
]
Patients slept on average 1.6 hours longer with the second drug. With only 10 patients, the confidence interval is wide, from about 0.7 to 2.5 hours: a clear effect, but an imprecise estimate of its size.

