The p-value is 0.003, so the faculties do differ in stress. The size of the difference is measured by #strong[eta squared] ($eta^2$), the share of all the variation in stress that lies between faculties:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("ss ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("summary");#NormalTok("(stress_anova)[[");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("]][[");#StringTok("\"Sum Sq\"");#NormalTok("]]");],
[#NormalTok("ss[");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("] ");#SpecialCharTok("/");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("sum");#NormalTok("(ss)");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("[1] 0.02715776");],));
]
