=== Costs of the two errors
<costs-of-the-two-errors>
Moving the threshold trades one error for the other, so the choice depends on how much each error costs. The costs are not statistical quantities; they are judgements about consequences, and they should be made explicitly. Suppose the counselling service judges that missing a student who is at risk is ten times as costly as an unnecessary conversation. The total cost of each threshold can then be calculated from the cross-validated predictions:

