== Time series data
<time-series-data>
Most of this book's methods assume that observations are independent: one student's answers tell you nothing about another's. In a time series the opposite is true. The number of visits this week is closely related to the number last week, and the order of the observations is essential. The methods of this chapter are built around that dependence.

