#ref(<fig-timeplot>, supplement: [Figure]) shows the parts of a pattern described above, and one feature the doctors did not mention. There is a #strong[seasonal pattern] that repeats every academic year: peaks before and during the two exam periods, dips during the breaks, and very few visits in the summer, when the service is reduced. There is a gentle upward #strong[trend], each year a little busier than the last, and there is #strong[noise], week-to-week variation that follows no pattern. Finally, there is one #strong[unusual week], in the autumn of 2023, far busier than the weeks around it.

=== Seasonal patterns
<seasonal-patterns>
A #strong[seasonal plot] puts the years on top of each other, so the seasonal pattern and the differences between years are easier to see. The academic year starts in September, so the weeks are numbered from the start of each academic year:

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("visits ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");],
