R's #NormalTok("co2"); dataset records the monthly concentration of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere, measured at the Mauna Loa observatory in Hawaii from 1959 to 1997: a famous series with a strong upward trend and a yearly cycle, as plants absorb CO#sub[2] in the northern summer. With a 12-month season, ETS and ARIMA can model the seasonal pattern directly. Training on the years to 1990 and testing on 1991 to 1997:

#block[
