The function #NormalTok("as_tsibble()"); converts R's older time series objects, and #NormalTok("h = \"7 years\""); gives the forecast horizon in words. Both ETS and ARIMA forecast seven years ahead with an average error (MAE) of only 1.0 and 1.2 parts per million, while the seasonal naive method, which ignores the trend, falls further behind every year.

